/*
================================================================================================================
GOLD LAYER VIEWS
================================================================================================================
This script creates the business-ready views in the GOLD layer of the data warehouse.
The GOLD layer is designed for reporting and analytics. It contains curated,
clean, and denormalized views that are easier for BI tools and end users to query
than the raw source tables in the silver layer.

VIEW USAGE:
- Views are reusable virtual tables that expose curated data without storing it again.
- They help abstract transformation logic and keep reporting queries simple.
- They improve maintainability because business logic is defined once and reused.
- They support analytical reporting by giving a clean star-schema-style structure.
- They allow downstream tools like Power BI, Tableau, and SQL reports to read
  reliable, business-friendly data.

In this script:
- dim_customers: customer dimension for customer-level analysis
- dim_products: product dimension for product/category analysis
- fact_sales: sales fact table for revenue and order analysis
================================================================================================================
*/

/*
================================================================================================================
View: gold.dim_customers
Description:
The customer dimension provides a cleaned and unified customer profile for reporting.
It combines customer details from CRM data, ERP demographic data, and location data.
This view is used to segment customers by geography, gender, date of creation, and marital status.

Business Usage:
- Customer segmentation and profiling
- Sales analysis by customer type and region
- Demographic analysis for campaigns and insights
- Customer-level KPI reporting

View comments:
- A view is a saved SQL query that acts like a table.
- It does not physically duplicate data, but it gives a stable logical table for reports.
- This is useful in a warehouse because transformations can be centralized and reused.
================================================================================================================
*/
CREATE OR ALTER VIEW gold.dim_customers AS
SELECT
     ROW_NUMBER() OVER(ORDER BY cst_id) customer_key,
     ci.cst_id customer_id,
     ci.cst_key customer_number,
     ci.cst_firstname first_name,
     ci.cst_lastname last_name,
     cc.cntry country,
     ci.cst_marital_status marital_status,
     CASE WHEN ci.cst_gndr != 'N/A' THEN ci.cst_gndr
       ELSE COALESCE(eci.gen, 'N/A')
     END gender,
     eci.bdate birth_date,
     ci.cst_create_date create_date
FROM silver.crm_cust_info ci
LEFT JOIN silver.erp_cust_az12 eci
ON ci.cst_key = eci.cid
LEFT JOIN silver.erp_loc_a101 cc
ON cc.cid = ci.cst_key;

/*
================================================================================================================
View: gold.dim_products
Description:
The product dimension provides a clean catalog of active products and their category details.
It combines product master data with product category metadata to support product-based analytics.
Only products that are currently active are included.

Business Usage:
- Product performance analysis
- Category and subcategory reporting
- Product line profitability analysis
- Inventory and sales trend analysis

View comments:
- Views simplify downstream reporting by exposing a logical table with final transformed columns.
- They support analytics users without requiring them to understand underlying source joins.
- This improves consistency because all reports pull from the same curated output.
================================================================================================================
*/
CREATE OR ALTER VIEW gold.dim_products AS
SELECT 
      ROW_NUMBER() OVER(ORDER BY p.prd_start_dt,p.prd_key) product_key,
      p.prd_id poduct_id,
      p.prd_key product_number,
      p.prd_nm product_name,
      p.cat_id category_id,
      sc.cat category_name,
      sc.subcat subcategory_name,
      sc.maintenance maintenance,
      p.prd_cost product_cost,
      p.prd_line product_line,
      p.prd_start_dt product_start_date
FROM silver.crm_prd_info p
LEFT JOIN silver.erp_px_cat_g1v2 sc
ON p.cat_id = sc.id
WHERE p.prd_end_dt IS NULL;

/*
================================================================================================================
View: gold.fact_sales
Description:
The sales fact view stores transactional sales records for business reporting.
It joins sales transactions to the product and customer dimensions to provide a star-schema-like model.
Each row represents an order-level sales fact, enabling aggregated analysis across product and customer dimensions.

Business Usage:
- Revenue and sales trend analysis
- Order quantity analysis
- Customer and product-level performance analysis
- KPI dashboards and executive reporting

View comments:
- Fact tables store measurable events; dimensions store descriptive attributes.
- Views allow fact tables to remain accessible and reusable without duplicating data.
- Reporting tools can query gold.fact_sales directly and join to dimensions for drill-down.
================================================================================================================
*/
CREATE OR ALTER VIEW gold.fact_sales AS
SELECT 
sl.sls_ord_num order_number,
pr.product_key,
cu.customer_key,
sl.sls_order_dt order_date,
sl.sls_ship_dt shipping_date,
sl.sls_due_dt due_date,
sl.sls_sales sales_amount,
sl.sls_quantity quantity,
sl.sls_price price
FROM silver.crm_sales_details sl
LEFT JOIN gold.dim_products pr
ON sl.sls_prd_key = pr.product_number
LEFT JOIN gold.dim_customers cu
ON sl.sls_cust_id = cu.customer_id;
